<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head><%- include('../partials/head') %></head>
<body>
<div class="app">
<%- include('../partials/sidebar') %>
<%- include('../partials/topbar') %>

  <div class="card">
    <div class="card-body">
      <p class="hint mt-0">
        <strong>Two questions, both answered from Search Console history.</strong>
        Freshness asks which pages have not been touched in a long time <em>and</em> are losing ground — the
        second clause is what makes the answer usable, since a list of pages older than a year is most of any
        real site. Decay is measured relative to the whole site, so a month when everything fell does not
        produce forty page-level refresh tasks.
      </p>
      <p class="hint" style="margin-bottom:0">
        <strong>Intent drift is the harder one.</strong> The topic has not changed but what people want from it
        has: a guide that ranked for "what is X" now gets impressions for "X vs Y" and "X pricing". Traffic
        often falls slowly enough that no alert fires, and the page reads perfectly well on inspection.
        Measured as Jensen-Shannon divergence over the impression-weighted query mix between two snapshots —
        symmetric, always finite, and bounded at 1 bit, so one threshold means the same thing on every page.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <%- include('_partials/brandpicker') %>

  <% if (brand) { %>
  <div class="card">
    <div class="card-head"><h3>Analyse freshness and drift</h3></div>
    <div class="card-body">
      <form method="POST" action="/ai-seo/freshness/run">
        <input type="hidden" name="brand_id" value="<%= brand.id %>">
        <div class="field-row">
          <label class="field">
            <span>Pages to examine <span class="muted">(highest-impression first)</span></span>
            <select name="max_pages">
              <option value="20">20</option>
              <option value="40" selected>40</option>
              <option value="80">80</option>
              <option value="150">150 — slow</option>
            </select>
          </label>
          <label class="field">
            <span>Drift threshold <span class="muted">(bits, 0-1)</span></span>
            <input type="number" name="drift_threshold" value="0.35" min="0.1" max="0.9" step="0.05">
          </label>
          <label class="field">
            <span>Treat as stale after</span>
            <select name="stale_days">
              <option value="180">180 days</option>
              <option value="365" selected>365 days</option>
              <option value="730">2 years</option>
            </select>
          </label>
        </div>
        <div class="checkbox-row">
          <label class="check">
            <input type="checkbox" name="want_ai" <%= aiAvailable ? 'checked' : 'disabled' %>>
            Ask the model to read each drifted page — seasonal noise, a re-angle, or a split?
            <% if (!aiAvailable) { %><span class="muted">— needs an Azure OpenAI credential</span><% } %>
          </label>
        </div>
        <div class="checkbox-row">
          <label class="check"><input type="checkbox" name="force" value="1"> Re-ask rather than reusing the cached reading</label>
        </div>
        <div class="btn-row">
          <button type="submit" class="btn" <%= perms.canWrite ? '' : 'disabled' %>>Analyse</button>
        </div>
        <% if (!brand.gsc_property) { %>
          <p class="hint">
            This brand has no Search Console property paired, so neither decay nor drift can be measured.
            <a href="/brands/<%= brand.id %>">Pair one</a> and let a nightly sync run — drift needs two query
            snapshots, which is roughly two weeks of history.
          </p>
        <% } %>
      </form>
    </div>
  </div>
  <% } %>

  <%- include('_partials/runs') %>

<%- include('../partials/sidebar-end') %>
<%- include('../partials/foot') %>
